  "tools": [
   {
    "name": "request_secret",
    "description": "Asks the user for a secret (an API key, a token, a password) in a masked box beside the transcript, so the value never enters the conversation. Answers the variable name and a placeholder of the form [secret-pane:NAME:xxxxxxxx], which becomes the real value inside a Bash command; the value is hidden again in everything that comes back. Write the placeholder in a Bash command where the value goes, as you would write the value: curl -H \"Authorization: Bearer <placeholder>\" https://..., API_KEY=<placeholder> npm test. A value holding characters the shell reads (a space, a quote, $...) goes in only as a whole single-quoted word, '<placeholder>', and the answer says which applies. A command is refused, with the reason and the fix, when it would put the value where it cannot be taken back (a git subcommand that writes history or sends it out, a gh command other than gh secret, a commit while a change holds the value) or runs in the background. No other tool restores a placeholder: Write and Edit refuse one. The value lives in this session's memory only: the mod writes nothing to disk, and a new session or /clear asks the user again. Use it in place of asking the user to paste a secret into the chat."
   }
